              "source_context": "In response to Israel's National Water Carrier, the Arab League resolved to divert the Banyas and Hasbani rivers to cut Israel's water supply by 35%. Between 1965 and 1966, Israeli tanks and aircraft repeatedly bombed the Syrian engineering construction sites, completely halting the diversion. Hinge Question: Why did Israel treat the Arab headwaters diversion project as a legitimate casus belli (act of war)?",
