          "viewing_task": "<ol><li><strong>[01:05] Recall:</strong> What was the military codename of the surprise Israeli pre-emptive air strike launched at 07:45 on the morning of 5 June 1967?</li><li><strong>[02:30] Explain:</strong> Explain how the destruction of over 300 Egyptian combat aircraft on the ground in the first three hours decided the entire outcome of the Six-Day War.</li><li><strong>[03:50] Challenge:</strong> By 10 June 1967, Israel had captured territories three times its original size. How did this astonishing victory transform Israel from a vulnerable state into an occupying power with complex demographic problems?</li></ol>",
          "model_answer": "<ol><li><strong>Recall:</strong> Operation Focus (<em>Mivtza Moked</em>).</li><li><strong>Explain:</strong> Achieving total air supremacy allowed Israeli Mirages and Super Mystères to act as flying artillery with complete freedom. Israeli ground forces advancing across Sinai, the West Bank, and the Golan Heights faced zero hostile air attacks, while retreating Egyptian, Jordanian, and Syrian armor was mercilessly pulverized from the air.</li><li><strong>Challenge:</strong> While conquering the Sinai, Gaza Strip, West Bank, East Jerusalem, and Golan Heights provided unprecedented geographical buffer zones, it brought over one million disenfranchised Palestinian Arabs under Israeli military control, creating a profound, permanent dilemma between democratic principles and demographic preservation.</li></ol>"
