            "prompt": "Use the structure strip and causal connectives below to structure your response.",
            "model": "Israeli military intervention began in March 1978 following the Fatah Coastal Road attack, when Prime Minister Menachem Begin launched Operation Litani. Over 25,000 Israeli troops advanced to the Litani River to push PLO artillery positions away from the northern Israeli border. Although UN Security Council Resolution 425 established UNIFIL peacekeepers and a Christian militia buffer zone, PLO rocket attacks resumed, convincing Defence Minister Ariel Sharon that only a total destruction of the PLO infrastructure in Lebanon could guarantee security.<br><br>The conflict escalated into total war in June 1982 following the attempted assassination of Israeli Ambassador Shlomo Argov in London. Sharon launched Operation Peace for Galilee, deceptively telling the Israeli cabinet the military would advance only 40 kilometres to create a safe zone. Instead, armoured columns drove sixty miles north to lay siege to West Beirut. For ten weeks, Israeli forces subjected the Lebanese capital to relentless artillery bombardment and air strikes, eventually forcing Yasser Arafat and thousands of PLO fighters to evacuate Lebanon under international supervision and relocate their headquarters to Tunis.<br><br>Finally, the operation culminated in moral and political catastrophe in September 1982. Following the assassination of Lebanese President-elect Bachir Gemayel, Israeli forces allowed Lebanese Christian Phalangist militias into the Sabra and Shatila refugee camps. Over three days, the militias slaughtered between 800 and 2,000 defenceless Palestinian civilians while the IDF fired illumination flares. The massacre triggered a massive demonstration of 400,000 people in Tel Aviv, and the subsequent Kahan Commission inquiry ruled Sharon bore personal responsibility, forcing his resignation. Ultimately, the Lebanon intervention fractured Israeli domestic consensus, cost hundreds of soldiers' lives, and bogged Israel down in an eighteen-year guerrilla war against the newly formed Hezbollah.",
