              "source_context": "Signed in Taba in September 1995, Oslo II divided the West Bank into three zones: Area A (major Palestinian cities, 18% of land, full PA control), Area B (Palestinian towns/villages, 22% of land, PA civil control/IDF security control), and Area C (Jewish settlements, military bases, Jordan Valley, 60% of land, exclusive Israeli control). Palestinians were left with fragmented islands surrounded by Israeli checkpoints. Hinge Question: How did the division of the West Bank into disconnected enclaves in Areas A and B hinder the emergence of a viable independent Palestinian state?",
