              "source_context": "To keep negotiations from collapsing, the architects of Oslo adopted a gradualist approach, leaving the most explosive issues—the status of Jerusalem, right of return for refugees, borders, and Israeli settlements—for 'final status' talks planned for 1999. In the interim, both Hamas suicide bombings and Israeli settlement expansion undermined public trust on both sides. Hinge Question: Why did the Oslo process defer final status issues (Jerusalem, refugees, borders, settlements) to later negotiations rather than resolving them immediately?",
