            "prompt": "Use the structure strip and causal connectives below to structure your response.",
            "model": "The peace process began to gather momentum in 1992 following the election of Israeli Prime Minister Yitzhak Rabin on a platform of territorial compromise. In complete secrecy, Israeli academics and PLO officials met in Norway for informal back-channel negotiations, culminating in the historic Letters of Mutual Recognition where Israel recognized the PLO and Arafat renounced terrorism. On 13 September 1993, Rabin and Arafat signed the Oslo I Accord on the White House lawn, agreeing to phased Palestinian self-government starting with Gaza and Jericho.<br><br>Following this initial breakthrough, negotiations expanded into implementation with the May 1994 Cairo Agreement and the October 1994 Israel-Jordan Peace Treaty. Arafat returned to Palestinian territory to establish the Palestinian National Authority (PNA). In September 1995, the parties signed the Oslo II Agreement, dividing the West Bank into Areas A (Palestinian civil and security control), B (Palestinian civil and joint Israeli security control), and C (exclusive Israeli control).<br><br>Finally, this fragile progress was shattered by escalating extremist violence from both sides. In February 1994, Jewish extremist Baruch Goldstein massacred 29 Muslim worshippers at the Cave of the Patriarchs in Hebron, prompting retaliatory suicide bus bombings by Hamas that turned Israeli public opinion against the peace process. The crisis culminated on 4 November 1995 when Jewish religious extremist Yigal Amir assassinated Prime Minister Rabin at a Tel Aviv peace rally. Consequently, Rabin’s murder shattered the political trust required for peace and brought the momentum of the Oslo peace process to a tragic halt.",
